module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.algebra_structure_has_two_representations_with_no_declared_mapping

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, WholeDeclaration }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data algebra_structure_has_two_representations_with_no_declared_mapping: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "algebra_structure_has_two_representations_with_no_declared_mapping" as NonEmptyStr,
  receipts: [
    "INVALID STATE: one algebraic structure is represented twice with no declared mapping between the representations (a DESIGN section 3 fork). HOME 1, std.algebra RECORD TYPES: `type OrderedRing<T> { add, sub, zero, negate, mul, .. compare, eq, lt .. }`, `BooleanAlgebra<T> { meet, join, complement, top, bottom }`, inhabited by std VALUES (v2.std.integer int_ordered_ring: OrderedRing<Int>, v2.std.logic bool_boolean_algebra: BooleanAlgebra<Bool>), which the language models' grounding rows cite (v2.extdeps.languages.cpp cpp_bool_grounding and its siblings). HOME 2, v2.std.algebra_structure_signature SIGNATURE NODES: ring_type_node, ordered_ring_type_node, lattice_type_node, boolean_algebra_type_node, whose operations are binder edges named ^ring_field_add, ^lattice_field_join, .. and which every language model's AlgebraInhabitanceDecl inhabits (v2.extdeps.languages.rust rust_integer_algebra_inhabitance, swift, java, lean). The OPERATOR vocabulary is home 2 (v2.std.compilers.target_model canonical_operation_op_add = AlgebraPrimitive { algebra_field: ^ring_field_add }), so a consumer that holds a home-1 instance cannot ask whether it carries an operator's field: nothing maps ^ring_field_add to OrderedRing.add.",
    "HARM: every consumer bridging the two invents its own mapping, a second authority each time, or picks one home and ignores facts stated in the other. Found while making v2 infer derive `||` through one algebra-operator route (N7-1): the instance facts for Int and Bool lived in home 1 and the operator fields in home 2, so the dag language model states its primitives in home 2 with a WITNESS citing the home-1 value (v2.extdeps.languages.dag dag_algebra_inhabitance_decls) rather than restating the fact; that keeps one statement of the inhabitance but does not join the structures. RUNG FOUND AT: mitigatable (no wrong answer is produced; consumers refuse or are absent). CEILING: structurally impossible -- one structure model. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, NAMING THE CAPABILITY: one structure model consumed by both the language models and std.algebra -- each structure declared once, its operations named once, and the record form (if kept) derived from the signature or vice versa -- SUFFICIENT FOR an instance stated in either place to answer an operator-field query with no consumer-local mapping.",
    "RECEIPT, XL-2 step 1 (collection concat), a DISPOSITION OF THE THIRD HOME, not a third coexisting one. The std.algebra template tables (free_monoid_collection_templates and siblings, AlgebraFieldTemplate rows) were a third representation of the collection operations. RULED SPLIT (calm-boar-904, msg_8e2338e7 and msg_702ad2cc): signature-world AlgebraInhabitanceDecl rows type OPERATORS only (v2.compiler.infer's binary-algebra arm, gunbc#13060); the std.algebra collection roster row is the SINGLE typing authority for collection operations (map, all, fold, concat), bound through v2.compiler.fold_lowering's ONE roster binder (collection_roster_rows) and typed from the row (collection_roster_signature_arrow), and nothing else reads the template tables a second time. That REVERSES the earlier joint ruling that a bare concat reaches its field only through an imported declaration and that infer never reads the template tables. REASON: the only writable declaration, a .dag body for std.algebra list_append, regresses every caller from the persistent carrier's log(n + m) to O(|left|) and makes v2.std.node's subtree-accumulating fold quadratic, and an operator-backed fn body has no writable surface (O5). CONSEQUENCE: the ^free_monoid_field_concat structure node and a FreeMonoid AlgebraInhabitanceDecl row were NOT built; nothing would consume them (DESIGN section 3c). The signature-world free-monoid node stays unbuilt until an operator names a free-monoid field.",
    "RECEIPT, XL-2 kernel-String concat (the follow-up to the collection concat receipt above): the signature-world FREE-MONOID STRUCTURE is now BUILT, because it gained a consumer. v2.std.algebra_structure_signature free_monoid_structure_type_node (its own binder ^free_monoid_field_concat, composing monoid_type_node -- the universal framework's free monoid, not a coined 'concatenation' structure, calm-boar-904) bounds the collection roster's concat carrier through the binder's one BinderTypeEdge (#13038's annotation carrier, read as a StructureBound by v2.std.type_binder type_param_bound, derived from the annotation and never a stored tag). v2.compiler.infer infer_application_structure_bounds admits the carrier's instance only through the ONE inhabitance authority, the AlgebraInhabitanceDecl rows (v2.extdeps.languages.dag dag_free_monoid_free_monoid_inhabitance, witness std.algebra list_append; dag_host_text_free_monoid_inhabitance, witness v2.std.node host_text_concatenation). So collection concat's TYPING stays the roster row's, and its CARRIER ADMISSION is the signature world's: one fact each, no third home. A monoid bound would have admitted Int (its ring composes an additive monoid); the free monoid excludes it. An AUTHORED structure bound in source still names a home-1 record and is judged as a kind at resolve: that is this row's mapping frontier, unchanged.",
  ],
  evidence: [
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.std.algebra_structure_signature", decl_name: "ordered_ring_type_node", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.std.integer", decl_name: "int_ordered_ring", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.std.logic", decl_name: "bool_boolean_algebra", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.extdeps.languages.dag", decl_name: "dag_algebra_inhabitance_decls", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.compiler.fold_lowering", decl_name: "collection_roster_signature_arrow", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "std.algebra", decl_name: "collection_concat_shape", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.std.algebra_structure_signature", decl_name: "free_monoid_structure_type_node", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.compiler.infer", decl_name: "infer_application_structure_bounds", field: WholeDeclaration },
  ],
}
